# Query: Drift Detection

Spec: QueryDriftDetection
Purpose:
  Detect all drift types between .sdd declarations and observed reality.

Query:
  show @drift
  where
    scope = <project>
    AND type = <structural|behavioral|contract|database|security|configuration|documentation|terminology>

  for each drift:
    classify: DECLARATION_WRONG | CODE_WRONG | BOTH_OUTDATED | UNKNOWN
    evidence: [<ids>]
    sync_op: SYNC_SDD | SYNC_CODE | SYNC_BOTH | NO_CHANGE | REVIEW

  output:
    drift_report:
      total_drifts: <n>
      by_type:
        structural: <n>
        behavioral: <n>
        contract: <n>
        database: <n>
        security: <n>
        configuration: <n>
        documentation: <n>
        terminology: <n>
      by_classification:
        declaration_wrong: <n>
        code_wrong: <n>
        both_outdated: <n>
        unknown: <n>
      items:
        - id: @drift.D<id>
          type: <type>
          classification: <classification>
          declared: <sdd excerpt>
          observed: <code excerpt>
          evidence: [<ids>]
          recommendation: <sync_op>
          confidence: <HIGH|MEDIUM|LOW>

SavedAs: @query:drift-detection

Navigation:
  Parent: @../INDEX.sdd
  DriftSpec: @../lifecycle/drift.sdd
  Architecture: @../architecture/INDEX.sdd
  Evidence: @../lifecycle/entity-schemas.sdd

State: +
